# What `composer require` downloads. Packagist builds its zipball from the tag
# with `git archive`, so this file is the dist.
#
# A line here can be wrong without anything in the repository noticing: no test
# fails, no build breaks, and the first person to find out is a consumer whose
# `vendor/` is missing something. tests/Unit/dist-archive.php asserts what the
# rules below produce, which makes this file the input and that test the check.
#
# The development half, none of which a consumer can run: the only dev dependency
# is the test framework, and it is not installed.
/.github            export-ignore
/tests              export-ignore
/tools              export-ignore
/examples           export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist   export-ignore
/smoke.php          export-ignore
/stress.php         export-ignore
/sonar-project.properties export-ignore

# Tracked, but not shipped. tools/build-phar.php copies the lock beside the
# manifest and installs with `--no-dev` there, which must resolve nothing, so the
# repository needs it. A consumer's install never reads it: Composer does not
# consult a dependency's lock, so it would arrive as a file of pins the install
# ignored, disagreeing with the versions actually installed.
/composer.lock      export-ignore
